Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Q-STALE-SWEEP-04: Stale constant detection with decay
 (18 tests)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements stale sweep module with:
- StaleSweep class: loads constants_config.json, computes staleness via (now - last_read) / half_life
- Staleness metric: float [0, ∞); staleness >= 1.0 triggers STALE gap callout
- ConstantStatus enum: ACTIVE, STALE, RETIRED with status transitions
- sweep() method: identifies stale constants and emits StaleGapCallout events
- re_read_constant(): resets last_read_at and status to ACTIVE
- retire_constant(): marks status RETIRED with timestamp
- Query methods: get_stale_constants(), get_active_constants()
- Export functions: export_staleness_report() and export_callouts() to JSONL
- Test coverage: 18 tests covering initialization, staleness computation, sweep execution, constant management, callout generation, queries, and export

All tests pass. Staleness computation validates against half_life_days and creates meaningful decay-based detection for molt cycle integration.

